<h2>What are CSS variables?</h2>
<hr>
<p>CSS variables (more formerly known as custom properties) are standardised values such as specific colours and numbers which can be reused throughout a project. We use CSS variables
  all over the website in several areas, ensuring that pk-gov's design is as consistent as possible. The CSS variables used in pk-gov can be found in the 'variables.css' file (located in styles/
  with the other .css files).
</p>
<h2>List of all pk-gov typography variables</h2>
<hr>
<h3>font-family</h3>
<p>There are two font-family variables available, which should be chosen according to the <a class="link" href="/dev/design/gov-identity/">Government identity guidelines</a>.</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>--plex-sans: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif;</code> sets the font-family of the styled element to IBM Plex Sans, with the default sans-serif font as a fallback.</li>
  <li><code>--mona-sans: 'Mona Sans', serif;</code> sets the font-family of the styled element to Mona Sans, with the default serif font as a fallback.</li>
</ul>